CREDIT

C4Lens is inspired by LikeC4 (https://likec4.dev, MIT License, Copyright (c)
2023-2026 Denis Davydkov), whose DSL and viewer set its direction. C4Lens reads
the same `.c4` syntax and `.likec4.snap` layout files and does not depend on
LikeC4. Its engine (src/engine), viewer (src/viewer) and MCP read tools
(src/mcp/read-tools) were written from LikeC4's public documentation and
observed behaviour under clean-room rules, not from its source;
docs/sdlc/engine/README.md records the process and the duplicate-code scan.

C4Lens versions up to 0.2.2 were built on LikeC4 as a dependency. Code written
in that period, notably the static SVG shapes in src/svg/shapes.ts, which
reproduce the look of LikeC4's element shapes, may contain material derived
from LikeC4. To the extent it does, it is used under LikeC4's MIT License:

